{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible. Since $C$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $C$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $Q=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ x & x\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "x=0"] ["math" "x=2"] ["math" "x=\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-11721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 3=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=4\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 12=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-127762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ and $C$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3x+2 & 2x-4\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1\\cdot (2x-4)-2\\cdot (3x+2) \\\\  & =2x-4-6x-4 \\\\  & =-4x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-8 & =0 \\\\ -4x & =8 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x+4 & 0 \\\\ 15 & -x-3\\end{aligned}]$\nbe a singular matrix. **In ascending order**, the values of $x$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x+4)\\cdot (-x-3)-0\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-6x-4x-12 \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}-10x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}-10x-12 & =0 \\\\ -2({x}^{2}+5x+6) & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6dfec28172520e24dfb5fac9e6d1db42228096620e675745f931faa32c6d1a6"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"} {"question" "q-316825" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033015/state.json" "file_sha256" "abab286f7ee12ab2959b062bb584b522e307d97c82288d7f52032f3fa9ab38fa"}] "usage" {"q-11718" []} "basis" 1227 "retractions" [[17592186087928 :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084580 17592186084581 17592186084582 17592186084583 17592186084584] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084579 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084579 :answer-field/id] [17592186084579 :answer-field/key] [17592186084579 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
